Description: Add locale stub for protoc-gen-js linking
 protoc-gen-js is a build tool that generates JavaScript bindings from
 Protocol Buffer files. It requires locale symbols from libc++ for iostream
 initialization, but the bundled libc++'s locale.cpp cannot be compiled on
 Debian due to type conflicts with glibc headers.
 .
 Missing symbols: std::__Cr::locale::*, std::__Cr::num_put::id,
 std::__Cr::ctype::id, __cxa_guard_*, __cxa_pure_virtual
 .
 This patch adds a minimal stub implementation (cef_locale_stub.cpp) that
 provides the necessary locale symbols for linking. Since protoc-gen-js is
 a build tool that runs with LC_ALL=C and only outputs generated code, it
 doesn't need actual locale functionality.
 .
 Build 135: locale.cpp compilation proven impossible (__newlocale conflicts)
 Build 163c-164: System libc++ failed (ABI namespace mismatch __Cr vs __1)
 Build 165: Stub approach (isolated, minimal, safe)
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <vejeta@gmail.com>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/915400
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-11-14

--- a/third_party/protobuf-javascript/BUILD.gn
+++ b/third_party/protobuf-javascript/BUILD.gn
@@ -12,6 +12,11 @@ if (current_toolchain == host_toolchain
       "src/generator/well_known_types_embed.cc",
       "src/generator/well_known_types_embed.h",
     ]
+
+    # Debian: Add locale stub for linking (avoids locale.cpp compilation issues)
+    sources += [
+      "//debian/cef_locale_stub.cpp",
+    ]
     include_dirs = [ "src" ]
     deps = [
       "//third_party/protobuf:protoc_lib",
